// Ad-Delivered PDF Site Access - Malvertising Risk
//
// Detects browser-initiated access to PDF-themed domains commonly abused
// in malvertising campaigns, where the destination URL contains online
// advertising identifiers (gclid, gad_source, gad_campaignid, campaign_id,
// adgroup_id, clickid).
//
// These sites frequently masquerade as legitimate PDF tools or document
// viewers and are used to redirect users toward malware, fake updates,
// or follow-on executable downloads.
//
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HOST-ANCHOR REGEX (why it is written this way):
//   url.address matches "https?://[^/]*pdf[^/]*\\.[a-z]{2,}/"
//
//   [^/]* before and after "pdf" keeps the match inside the HOST only --
//   the first "/" ends the host, so "pdf" appearing later in a path or
//   query string (e.g. /manual.pdf) will NOT match. This preserves the
//   original intent of requiring "pdf" in the domain itself.
//
//   \\.[a-z]{2,}/ is a GENERIC TLD anchor (any 2+ letter TLD: com, ai,
//   app, io, xyz, etc.) followed by the host-terminating slash. This
//   replaces the earlier hard-coded ".com" anchor, which blinded the rule
//   to malvertising domains on cheap non-.com TLDs (e.g. pdfmaestro.ai).
//   A generic TLD anchor is used instead of a TLD allowlist because
//   throwaway malvertising domains are spun up on arbitrary cheap TLDs
//   and cannot be enumerated.
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// AD-IDENTIFIER BLOCK:
//   Google Ads now stamps gad_source / gad_campaignid in addition to the
//   legacy gclid. Both the gad_* params and gclid are required here so the
//   rule fires on current Google-Ads-driven malvertising. clickid /
//   campaign_id / adgroup_id are retained for non-Google ad networks.
//
// PRECISION NOTE:
//   The host regex alone is intentionally broad (any pdf-in-host domain on
//   any TLD). Precision comes from the AND with the ad-identifier block --
//   legitimate PDF services (e.g. Adobe createpdf.acrobat.com) are visited
//   without ad-click params and therefore do not fire. Confirmed-benign
//   domains that DO carry ad params should be added to the exclusion block.
//
// EXCLUSIONS:
//   The exclusions below represent PDF-related domains that are already
//   blocked or otherwise controlled in this environment, plus confirmed
//   -benign high-volume PDF services. This significantly reduces noise.
//   Each organization should review alert results and add their own
//   environment-specific exclusions as needed.
//   (Severity: Info -- this rule is known-noisy by design.)

event.category = "url"
AND event.url.action = "GET"
AND (
    url.address matches "https?://[^/]*pdf[^/]*\\.[a-z]{2,}/"
) AND (
    url.address contains "clickid="
    OR url.address contains "campaign_id"
    OR url.address contains "adgroup_id"
    OR url.address contains "gclid"
    OR url.address contains "gad_source"
    OR url.address contains "gad_campaignid"
) AND NOT (
    url.address contains "utm_campaign="
    OR url.address contains "utm_medium=email"
    // Example blocked / controlled / confirmed-benign PDF domains -- replace with your own
    OR url.address contains "YOURBLOCKEDDOMAINHERE.com"
    OR url.address contains "YOURBLOCKEDDOMAINHERE2.com"
    OR url.address contains "YOURBLOCKEDDOMAINHERE3.com"
)
